"One of the vehicles coming into the premises transported 1320 pieces of quail eggs of unfamiliar descent, moreover in inappropriate conditions.
Also, these eggs will be disposed of in a redevelopment enterprise," the State Veterinary Administration said.
When inspecting a live fish stall, it was then found that the seller does not have proof of the origin of the goods and is not registered for the sale of live fish.
The market is considered problematic from a veterinary point of view for a long period of time.
For example, last autumn veterinarians uncovered an illicit grocery store, almost half a tons of unlabelled groceries unrecognizing food.
For the majority it was not possible to determine the expiration date, some of the products had an expiration date and was spoiled.
For five kilograms of sepia, the expiration date was exceeded by three years.
