Approximately 2500 people currently work at TPCA and the company represents one of the largest exporters in the Czech Republic and at the same time an employer in the Kolín region.
Coffin Kills Bride Shortly After Weg of ambuimiate: Leave a Message to Her Tongue
Gemma Sisson has been battling for more insidious cancer for more than two years, and when she appeared to have defeated the cancer, the disease spoke again.
Thirty-nine-year-old woman who loved bodybuilography eventually ended up in a hospice in a hospice, where she still managed to take the love of her life.
Unfortunately, she succumbed to the disease.
A few hours after her death, a shocking message for those closest to her Facebook account emerged.
Gemma Sisson came from Leeds, England, loved bodybuilding.
With her friend Ricky Moore, with whom she had lived for more than 16 years, they have traveled for competitions all over the world.
A thirty-nine-year-year-old woman played sports and lived a healthy life, yet she was diagnosed with cancer in April 2018.
Gemma began exhaustive treatment, radiotherapy, in the hope that she will recover.
After months of under-treatment, Gemma really seemed to win over the cancer, but in August 2019 the cancer returned and this time the spine invaded the spine.
The bodybuilder and personal trainer underwent a ten-hour spine spine operation and then relaunched drastic treatment.
Of course, everything was in vain.
Earlier this year, at her thirty-ninth birthday, doctors informed her that she had a few months to live.
In early April, a handsome blonde finally decided to go into a hospice in Leeds, where she was visited every now and then by her family, who even gave her a wedding with her love Ricky.
The marriage lasted two months.
Ricky took Gemma for their two-month anniversary.
Four days later Gemma died in his arms.
Just a few hours after she died, a post Gema wrote for her family appeared on her social media account.
“Whether this has been published, it means that I have finally died after weeks of too much fighting.
Even though my heart will be heartbroken to leave my loved ones here, I will be so happy to get rid of what this terrible disease has done to me.
I can’t thank Ricky, who was by my side all the time and gave me a huge amount of love and support during that terrible time.”
"I'm also thankful for all the support I've received from all my followers on the social network," she wrote, noting that everyone should respect their lives and live them to the fullest.
