A deposit of 3.5 million for an apartment in Brno, however, it was paid from Rafaj's account.
Rafaj has been the Chairman of the Office for the Protection of Competitiveness since 9 July 2009, for the second term of office the President of the Former Social Democrat Deputies in June 2015.
In less than a year, Rafaj's second six-year-old mandate expires.
An anti-monopoly bureau law stipulates that the president can dismiss the chairmanship of the office at a suggestion of the government.
It can only be revoked if it does not act for more than less than six Months or significantly undermines the dignity of its function or the independence and impartiality of office.
