This is mainly due to an increase in demand for European destinations, which now accounts for about 85 per cent of sales.
However, prices themselves are also deciphering in some European places, for example to Spain or Italy fell by about one-fifth in the past few weeks.
Crisis has also affected the behavior of customers, who now buy airfares far less in advance than before, because they are concerned about the further development of the coronavirus situation.
According to earlier Kiwi.com's flight purchase time before departure decreased by about ten days year-on-year.
"This confirms the future trend, when people will order air tickets much less in advance, they will require more flexibility, take less risks," said Michal Šindelář, vice president for Kiwi.com products.
At the same time, the average booking time is 21 days.
Together with the growth of sales, the number of renewed air routes from the Czech Republic is also increasing.
There are currently regular flights to more than 60 destinations at the Prague airport.
Compared to last summer's, it is about half of the destinations.
