Karel Gott didn't like Vaclav Havel?!
Daughter Dominika Revealed
"Dad didn't have to him for many years," the eldest Daughter of Gotta Dominika told Aha!, adding that the Master couldn't come up with a name for Havl's and whenever it came up to him, it was always annoying Karl.
It's hard to say what they've done, according to Dominika, the controversy began sometime in the mid-1990's.
"Dad said in an article after the revolution that he had it easier than him.
That Havel could have written into a drawer at the time of the darkness, but if he somehow defied, he had an end with his career," Gottová said.
Immediately he adds that in the end the Czech greats found their way to each other.
"I don't know the word Havel couldn't even hear until his sixtieth birthday.
But then the president congratulated him with a letter for his birthday, and suddenly his father's relationship with him began to change," Dominika recalled.
After all, ten years later, Gott even invited the former president to celebrate his 70th birthday at the Ambassador Hotel on Wenceslas Square.
"And that's where a new era of their relationship began, because his father then regularly invited Mr. Havla home to Bertramka," added the blonde, whose father died last October.
The Nightingale is also said to have regretted that he had never received a state award from Vaclav Havel.
After all, however, he received it in 2009, even though it was already from the hands of his successor as Vaclav Klaus (79).
Another honor will come in memoriam, the current president Miloš Zeman (75) is supposed to award him the Order of the White Lion and thus honor his memory.
As of Tuesday there is a threat of heat in the Czech Republic, meteorologists warn of fires
Meteorologist warnings against high temperatures apply to Tuesday afternoon for the whole of Bohemia, with the exception of the Karlovy Vary region, as well as for southern and central Moravia.
"Exceptionally, temperatures can also exceed 34 degrees Celsius, especially in Central Bohemia," they say.
People are advised to maintain a drinking regime in the heat and limit the physical load in noon and afternoon.
Due to the warm weather with a minimum of rainfall, there will be a risk of fires from Tuesday morning.
Windy weather could contribute to their rapid proliferation.
The warning of meteorologists against the risk of fires concerns Central Bohemia, including Prague, Liberec, Ústecký, the Karlovy Vary and Pilsen regions.
A warning against fires will come into force until further notice.
"Significant rainfall, which would allevigate the danger, in the northwest and west of Bohemia, is not expected at least by the end of the week," the CHMI said.
The Prague municipality reacted to the warning of meteorologists by banning making fires in high-hazardous places, which is supposed to take effect from Tuesday.
People in the capital won’t be able to establish open fires, for example, in parks, gardens or forests, up to a distance of up to 50 meters from the outskirts.
Smoking and the use of pyrotechnology are also prohibited in these places.
The measure will apply until further notice, Prague City Hall spokesman Vít Hofman said.
